Subject: Tweak: secure stadiums
Upstream-base: 9046e67aa2077a7eb4ed6e28c9df3c1d3b368f84

The game's Secure Stadium cheat (ENV_CHEAT_SECURE) stops every stadium's
weather: GameInfoManager::IsRule0x4Equal1 is the one test, and with it
Weather::Update never starts one. No lightning, no wind (nor Thunder
Island's debris), no solar flares, no bubbling lava, no Storm Ship tilt, and
no Thwomps or sand patches in the Sand Tomb. The electric fences stay: the
cheat leaves the walls alone, and Thunder Island walls applies with it. The
game honours the cheat in offline Domination, when chosen in its cheats
menu, and in matches that carry their own rules (UseAltRules).

With "Secure stadiums" enabled, the cheat holds in every offline match but
the Striker Challenges, which keep their own rules; Strikers 101 keeps the
game's (never). Online matches are left alone: both games would have to
agree on it, which the tweak bits cannot say.

diff --git a/src/Game/GameInfo.cpp b/src/Game/GameInfo.cpp
index 963cddb..68e7031 100644
--- a/src/Game/GameInfo.cpp
+++ b/src/Game/GameInfo.cpp
@@ -566,6 +566,14 @@ bool GameInfoManager::IsRule0x4Equal1() const
         return false;
     }
 
+#if defined(MSCHARGED_TWEAKS)
+    // Port tweak "Secure stadiums": the game's Secure Stadium cheat in every
+    // offline match but the Striker Challenges. Online matches are left alone.
+    if (mscharged_tweak_enabled(MSCHARGED_TWEAK_SECURE_STADIUMS) && !IsOnline() && mCurrentMode != GM_CHALLENGE) {
+        return true;
+    }
+#endif
+
     if ((mIsOnlineMode == 0 && mCurrentMode == GM_FRIENDLY) || UseAltRules()) {
         return GetActiveRules()->mEnvironmentCheat == ENV_CHEAT_SECURE;
     }
